content.content:
## decisions
- {"decision": "Architecture: K districts, each a separate ACL9SiteMap actor that runs the UNCHANGED generator (CL9SiteLayout::Generate) on its own sub-seed, module count and world transform. Add FCL9SiteDistrict {Offset (cm from the truck pad), Yaw in {0,90,180,270}, ModuleCount (base), Zones (empty = use the site Zones)} and TArray<FCL9SiteDistrict> Districts on UCL9SiteDef. When Districts is empty, the current single-site path runs byte-identical, so henhouse, farm and pigfarm do not change.", "rationale": "There are few consumers, and I verified each one: GameMode::SpawnNight (CL9GameMode.cpp:504-646), GameState Rebuild/Clear (CL9GameState.cpp:401,405) and Cheats (CL9Cheats.cpp:46,73). Each turns into a loop. With one actor per district, ISM components are per district for free (CL9SiteMap.cpp:400-426, 656-683). That bounds the per-tile instance scan in Recast's nav gather (verified at InstancedStaticMeshComponentHelper.h:148-167) and the quadratic PlaceProps warning loop (CL9SiteMap.cpp:759-783) to farm scale times K. The 200-module behaviour proven by CL9.Map.LargeSite stays valid, and the 128 cap is never approached.", "rejected": "Generator lens: multi-root growth in one grid. It needs changes to the placement core (owner mask in Fits, trunk phase, MainCount from the budget at cpp:540, per-district Specials at cpp:554-572, open-yard rules in BuildSegments). Nobody has measured it at N >= 1000. It would still need district-keyed ISM components to fix the nav gather. It is strictly more code and risk than looping 5 consumers. Also rejected: a 'stitch K layouts into one' variant, which needs the same rotation work plus a trunk generator."}
- {"decision": "Grid cap row: keep the cap at 128 and do not touch it. The largest district at day 10 is 230 x 1.25 = 288 modules, which gives Span = ceil(sqrt(1728))*2 = 84 cells.", "rationale": "Under the district design no layout comes near 128. The generator lens is right that raising the cap would be harmless, but nothing needs it, so it is not done.", "rejected": "Raising the cap to 256 or deriving it from the budget (only needed for the single-grid design)."}
- {"decision": "Generation row: every machine generates K layouts from sub-seeds derived from the one replicated seed: SubSeed_i = HashCombine(Seed, i), with 0 remapped to 1, because Seed 0 builds nothing (CL9SiteLayout.cpp:842). Log LayoutHash and build ms per district. Add a scoped per-phase timer to ACL9SiteMap::Build (Generate / segments / props+lamps / register). Keep the synchronous build. The fallback, if the measured build hitch is over the budget the user sets (see unresolved), is to build one district per frame during the lobby.", "rationale": "Only one seed is replicated (CL9GameState.cpp:382-407). Sub-seeds keep determinism with no new replication. The build runs at lobby entry, not at night start (CL9GameMode.cpp:206-212, 270-271, 765-773). The panel verified this, which corrects the draft.", "rejected": "Async or streamed generation before anyone has measured a single-frame build."}
- {"decision": "District rotation: support Yaw in multiples of 90 degrees by spawning each district actor with its yaw. Change SiteToWorld to GetActorTransform().TransformPosition (CL9SiteMap.cpp:238-242). Spawn the flap with the actor's rotation and pass it the world-rotated Outward (CL9SiteMap.cpp:465-468). Nothing else needs to change: all ISM instances are local (AddInstance bWorldSpace=false at CL9SiteMap.cpp:504, 549, 567, 786), components and lamps are attached to the root (:422, :679, :802), and night spawns use random yaw, with jars at a zero rotator.", "rationale": "Without yaw every gate faces west (CL9SiteLayout.cpp:889, 906-908). Districts would then stack in one N-S column, the yard distances L reach 400-600 m, and 1,000 modules cannot fit the 600 s walk budget. Rotation lets the districts sit as a cross around the truck.", "rejected": "A whole-layout rotation pass inside the generator (generator lens). Actor yaw does the same thing with two small edits."}
- {"decision": "District count, size and placement: 5 districts on fixed slots in the stage JSON, with the seed filling only their contents. Initial slots: East (yaw 0) and West (yaw 180) at about 230 base modules each with gates at L of about 10-30 m; North and South (yaw 90/270) at about 190 each with L of about 210 m; one far district at about 160 with L of about 300 m. That sums to about 1,000 base modules (user decision 1). Size rule per district, from stage.md:58-59 with NightLength 600 and MainPathShare 0.30: 1.59*N_i + 0.444*L_i <= 440 (one-way yard distance L in metres at 4.5 m/s). Slots may not overlap as rotated day-10 span rectangles. Final offsets are set after the footprint measurement.", "rationale": "The project applies the night formula at base count; farm is 480 s at base 200 and gets no day-10 correction, because NightLengthCurve is flat. Every district can then be raided to its deep zone and back within one night, while all five clearly cannot (user decisions 2 and 3). Near districts are larger and far ones smaller and denser. Fixed slots satisfy both the nav lens (deterministic bounds) and the play lens (walk budget).", "rejected": "Equal 5 x 200 districts: N/S and far districts would break the 600 s budget. The play lens example also misstated that its sizes hold on day 10 (230 at L=10 gives 1.99*230 > 440). The project convention is base count, so the sizes are kept but applied at base."}
- {"decision": "Truck and yard: one truck pad, the existing ACL9TruckPad, at the yard centre. It anchors every district actor (pad + rotated offset). The yard is the level's bare floor plane, scaled by setup_stage.py to the union of rotated day-10 district rectangles plus MARGIN. There are no generated yard modules, no yard content and no yard monsters in the first cut.", "rationale": "This is the smallest change. setup_stage already scales the Floor/Ground actors (setup_stage.py:169-196). A generated yard would add fenced paddocks (CL9SiteLayout.cpp:1072-1113) or a large Grid instance count for nothing. Monsters are leashed to HomeRange (CL9Monster.cpp:1130-1132, 1240-1241), so an empty yard costs no AI.", "rejected": "Yards made of yard_open modules, open-yard segment rules and a new road row in the 'henhouse' theme, which would change the henhouse/farm/pigfarm pools."}
- {"decision": "Entrances and exits: each district keeps the generator's own yard_gate (Start, facing the truck after yaw) and its own single flapIn at its deepest dead end. Record in docs/decisions.md that module.md decision 3 ('one entrance, one flap') applies per district building, and that the truck docks at the stage pad rather than at each gate.", "rationale": "User decision 3 makes districts separate building clusters, and each one has to be enterable. One entrance plus one fire exit per building matches the Lethal-interior analogue that module.md:193-195 cites. It costs no code, because the generator already does it per layout (CL9SiteLayout.cpp:906-908, 969), and the four one-flap test assertions stay valid per layout.", "rejected": "One entrance and one flap for the whole stage. Only the single-grid design can express that, and it makes the far districts reachable only through the near ones."}
- {"decision": "Depth zones: depth is evaluated per district (per-layout hop normalisation, CL9SiteLayout.cpp:1201-1217, unchanged). Districts differ through an optional per-district Zones override (reusing FCL9SiteZone); an empty override uses the site Zones. Far districts get heavier rows (more pig, raccoon and meat). ValueRate stays 1.0.", "rationale": "This answers the generator lens objection that per-district normalisation makes every district identical. It reuses the existing struct and the existing SpawnNight zone loop (CL9GameMode.cpp:600-613), called once per district.", "rejected": "Global hop depth across one grid (needs the single grid). Also a new per-district danger tier or DepthBias column, which is extra data on top of the Zones override."}
- {"decision": "Nav row: keep dynamic runtime navmesh with the default TileSizeUU 1000 and no invokers. setup_stage.py sizes ONE NavMeshBoundsVolume to the union of district rectangles plus margin, so the yard is navmeshed and the truck-to-gate paths can be checked. On the host, StartNight defers itself with a retry timer while the navigation build is in progress, and logs the wait. This needs no UI.", "rationale": "The map and its nav build happen in the lobby (CL9GameMode.cpp:270-271, 765-773). Nothing currently waits for nav before night start, and that gap is the real failure mode. With per-district ISM components, empty yard tiles scan no instances. Invokers either violate decision 4 or move the build into the night, and they are a global setting that would also change the other stages. The current code path stays: one box, just bigger.", "rejected": "Navigation invokers (violate decision 4 or move the build into the night). Per-slot volumes with no yard navmesh: kept as the fallback if the union build is too slow, because the union box is the existing path and makes the yard testable. A larger tile size up front: only after measurement."}
- {"decision": "Rendering row: no HLOD and no district distance or visibility culling system in the first cut. Per-district actors give per-district components, so frustum and occlusion culling works per district. Log the lamp count and the flicker-lamp count next to the existing build log lines (CL9SiteMap.cpp:630-635). The fallback, only if yard-view GPU Lights/VolumetricFog is over budget, is MaxDrawDistance on lamps plus skipping TickFlicker beyond it (CL9SiteMap.cpp:286-303, 789-818). LampDensity stays the total-count lever.", "rationale": "performance.md:22/94 forbid optimisation before measurement. Collision must stay on every district on the server because far monsters walk against WorldStatic (decision 4). Ray tracing is already distance-culled at 300 m.", "rejected": "Per-district show/hide (it does not remove physics or nav cost, and toggling re-creates instance bodies). HLOD."}
- {"decision": "Host monster cost under decision 4: AI, senses and movement always run. The monster MeshComponent sets VisibilityBasedAnimTickOption = OnlyTickMontagesWhenNotRendered in C++ (only the player overrides it today, at CL9Character.cpp:147). No think-rate LOD and no distance sleep.", "rationale": "No CL9 C++ uses montages or notifies, and the only bone read is the cosmetic hit puff (CL9Monster.cpp:405). Movement is code-driven (AddActorWorldOffset), so skipping unseen poses does not change behaviour. OnlyTickMontages is chosen over OnlyTickPose in case a Blueprint uses montage notifies. Skeletal animation is the largest per-monster item (performance.md:118-119).", "rejected": "Think-rate LOD by distance. It can be read as distance throttling against decision 4, so if the measurement fails the fallback is lowering counts, not throttling."}
- {"decision": "Population row and monster total: per district, roughly one Lethal interior. Base zone sums are about 9 (East/West), 11 (North/South) and 13 (far), about 53 in total. Through the existing MonsterCountCurve (0.6 on day 1, 1.0 on day 5, 1.5 on day 10, progression.md:29) that gives about 32 monsters on day 1, about 53 on day 5 and about 80 on day 10. Per district on day 10 that is about 13-20, against Titan's indoor 18 power at 1-3 power per enemy (lethal-map.md:204, lethal-monsters.md:595-629). Items keep the farm's per-module density (about 0.35 per module at base, farm.json:26-28), with far overrides weighted toward meat. Night spawning stays synchronous until it is measured; the fallback is time-sliced spawning.", "rationale": "This is a compromise between the nav-ai lens (about 45 / 80) and the play lens (35-40 / 90-100). It uses only existing data (Zones x day curve), with no new power system. It is about one third of a blind 5x of the farm (125 / 300), which user decision 4 rules out.", "rejected": "A Lethal-style power budget and spawn ramp (new code). 5x the farm density."}
- {"decision": "Night row: NightLength 600, DarkBase 450, DarkMin 300 (the farm's 360/240 scaled by 600/480). One night, no multi-trip.", "rationale": "User decision 2. It keeps DarkMin <= DarkBase <= NightLength (stage.md:53), and the district size rule keeps every district within one night.", "rejected": "30-50 min nights (from the original spec estimate)."}
- {"decision": "Walk-time row: do not add vehicles or shortcuts. Walk time is bounded by the per-district size rule plus jars. It is validated by a scripted walk truck -> gate -> deepest point -> nearest jar -> truck for each district.", "rationale": "The formula comes from only two data points (stage.md:58-59), so it must be checked by measurement.", "rejected": "Moving the truck, or several trips per night."}
- {"decision": "Return jars row: SpecialCopies (the existing site column, inherited as 4 from farm) applies per district, because each layout reads Params.SpecialCopies. That gives about 4 delivery rooms per district, about 20 in all. The jar dedupe set in SpawnNight resets per district, since module indices are per layout (CL9GameMode.cpp:625-633).", "rationale": "This needs no new data and it already works per layout (CL9SiteLayout.cpp:529, 556).", "rejected": "Reinterpreting SpecialCopies as per-district in a single grid."}
- {"decision": "Relevancy: keep the default NetCullDistance (150 m) and do not make monsters always relevant. Measure the client hitch when crossing between districts in 2-client PIE.", "rationale": "Client cost stays bounded. Today no CL9 actor overrides it (CL9ActorBase.cpp:9).", "rejected": "Raising the cull distance up front."}
- {"decision": "QA and tests: (1) CL9.Map.Districts: 30 seeds at each slot's day-10 module count (max 288); assert build, IsConnected, no overlap, one flap, at least 2 delivery rooms and at least 90% of budget; log ms and the occupied bounding box. (2) Slot test on the giant row: rotated day-10 rectangles do not overlap and every L_i satisfies the size rule. (3) Existing LargeSite and DepthBand stay unchanged as the guard that Districts-empty output is identical. (4) qa_farm_stage_pie.py: take the nav window from the union bounds instead of the hard-coded -10..400 / +-200 m (qa_farm_stage_pie.py:141-143); record nav-done seconds, monster state counts per sample, ever-moved, and the build-log counts (lamps included). (5) perf_probe spots: lobby-day yard, night yard facing the districts, and the deepest district interior, after first taking a Lvl_Farm baseline at equivalent spots.", "rationale": "The current script cannot gate a 1 km stage (render lens, verified line references). LargeSite only covers 200 modules.", "rejected": "Running layout tests at 1,000 modules in one layout, which tests a code path this design never runs."}
